(4643833, 665482, 51538, '<td valign="top">I voted a 6.  But for me I did not feel comfortable with the redishness of the face or the expanse of the foam.  I think I might have preferred a slightly desaturated image which was cropped much more closely to the subject''s face.  Perhaps even in a rich monochrome or duotone.  Not that I know anything about nothing, of course. ;-)</td>', 'I voted a 6.  But for me I did not feel comfortable with the redishness of the face or the expanse of the foam.  I think I might have preferred a slightly desaturated image which was cropped much more closely to the subject''s face.  Perhaps even in a rich monochrome or duotone.  Not that I know anything about nothing, of course. ;-)', '2008-04-16 13:49:29.000000', NULL, 0),
(4643847, 665482, 61971, '<td valign="top">I didn''t vote on this one, but it would have probably been a 4 or 5 from me. The head could be straight but even with that it would still look freeky. (although I must say Charlie is a cutie :).. ) Way too much negative space for me and it does seem blown out. It takes a while to get that it is bubbles. So I would have really liked this if you had gotten a little more up close and personal with some softer lighting, and maybe a conversion to black and white. jmo</td>', 'I didn''t vote on this one, but it would have probably been a 4 or 5 from me. The head could be straight but even with that it would still look freeky. (although I must say Charlie is a cutie :).. ) Way too much negative space for me and it does seem blown out. It takes a while to get that it is bubbles. So I would have really liked this if you had gotten a little more up close and personal with some softer lighting, and maybe a conversion to black and white. jmo', '2008-04-16 13:55:06.000000', NULL, 0),
(4643848, 667246, 74559, '<td valign="top">Fantastic image Timothy! Congrats on your new high score, this is so NOT just another flower picture! I''d have this on my wall any day :-)</td>', 'Fantastic image Timothy! Congrats on your new high score, this is so NOT just another flower picture! I''d have this on my wall any day :-)', '2008-04-16 13:55:38.000000', NULL, 0),
(4643862, 667210, 88688, '<td valign="top">well hurrah... a personal best... :-D  *insert wry grin* well, at least now I know what to improve on... pretty much everything...</td>', 'well hurrah... a personal best... :-D  *insert wry grin* well, at least now I know what to improve on... pretty much everything...', '2008-04-16 13:58:55.000000', NULL, 0),
(4644061, 667113, 81852, '<td valign="top">Congrats!  Excellent job! I''m very happy for you.</td>', 'Congrats!  Excellent job! I''m very happy for you.', '2008-04-16 15:17:35.000000', NULL, 0),
(4644067, 665482, 42198, '<td valign="top">I didn''t vote on this challenge - but here''s a bit of up-front technical critique as you requested in the forums :)<br/> <br/>- Composition: The shape looks too ''long'' and the face is too small in the center. A squarer frame cropped closer to the face might''ve worked better. Also, the space at the top and bottom draws my eye to the weird vignetting effect in the corners.<br/> <br/>- Colour/Contrast: His face looks too orange. The bubbles appear blown out with no real texture visible. Contrast is a bit high as well, giving his skin a blotchy look.<br/> <br/>- Focus: Face is too small in the frame, but it gives the impression his eyes aren''t in sharpest focus.<br/> <br/>I''m reminded of a shot by Judi, which I''ll post here for reference;<br/> <br/><a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/image.php?IMAGE_ID=485051" rel="nofollow" target="_blank"><img alt="'' . substr(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_challenge/0-999/650/120/485051.jpg'', strrpos(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_challenge/0-999/650/120/485051.jpg'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//images.dpchallenge.com/images_challenge/0-999/650/120/485051.jpg"/></a> <br/> <br/></td>', 'I didn''t vote on this challenge - but here''s a bit of up-front technical critique as you requested in the forums :) - Composition: The shape looks too ''long'' and the face is too small in the center. A squarer frame cropped closer to the face might''ve worked better. Also, the space at the top and bottom draws my eye to the weird vignetting effect in the corners. - Colour/Contrast: His face looks too orange. The bubbles appear blown out with no real texture visible. Contrast is a bit high as well, giving his skin a blotchy look. - Focus: Face is too small in the frame, but it gives the impression his eyes aren''t in sharpest focus. I''m reminded of a shot by Judi, which I''ll post here for reference;   ', '2008-04-16 15:19:29.000000', NULL, 0),
(4644104, 666364, 57060, '<td valign="top">Heini, thanks for your kind comment and congrats to you on a beautiful image as well. I hope to learn how to do a studio shot like this at some point, there is certainly alot more to this than meets the eye.<br/> <br/>Jack</td>', 'Heini, thanks for your kind comment and congrats to you on a beautiful image as well. I hope to learn how to do a studio shot like this at some point, there is certainly alot more to this than meets the eye. Jack', '2008-04-16 15:30:11.000000', NULL, 0),
